  "renderings": {
   "markdown": "# The Larkmoor Flood Relief Fund\n\n*documentary · factual · published as Example Desk · E09:document:9d82199f-13b1-468b-909d-8bcad7aad1a1@1 · draft*\n\n## The water rises\n\nAfter the river Ost flooded the invented town of Larkmoor, the relief fund collected sixty thousand. [verified_fact] [^1]\n\nTomas Brandt stood at the pump house door and counted the sandbags twice. [reconstruction] [^2]\n\n> Disclosure (reconstruction): This scene is reconstructed from committee minutes; gestures and wording are approximate.\n\nWe were told the fund was full. [attributed_testimony — Mirela Novak, shopkeeper] [^3]\n\n## The ledger\n\nOne transfer of 31,000 has no receipt in the ledger. [verified_fact] [^1]\n\nIt is not known who authorised the transfer. [unknown_acknowledged]\n\n## Sources\n\n[^1]: E07:claim:c-ledger@2\n[^2]: E05:evidence_version:ev-minutes@1\n[^3]: E06:segment:seg-novak-3@1\n\n## Credits\n\n- Written by Ines Varga (writer)\n"
  }
