  "renderings": {
   "markdown": "# The Larkmoor Fund (short film)\n\n*documentary · factual · published as Example Desk · E09:document:bb33fbe8-5c1e-4f59-a745-758ed8ee520a@1 · draft*\n\n### Scene: Show the record [verified_fact] [^1]\n\nCouncil archive · Day\n\nThe ledger lies open on the archive table.\n\n1. Slow move across ledger page 14 — close — 5s — assets: E05:evidence_version:ev-ledger@1\n\n(narration) One transfer of thirty one thousand has no receipt. [verified_fact] [^1]\n\n(on_screen_text) 31,000 unaccounted [verified_fact] [^1]\n\n### Scene: Show the night of the flood [reconstruction] [^2]\n\nPump house · Night\n\nA man counts sandbags by lamplight.\n\n1. Sandbags stacked against the door — 4s\n\n> Disclosure (reconstruction): Staged reconstruction of the night at the pump house.\n\n**Shopkeeper** (dialogue) We were told the fund was full. [attributed_testimony — Mirela Novak, shopkeeper] [^3]\n\n## Sources\n\n[^1]: E07:claim:c-ledger@2\n[^2]: E05:evidence_version:ev-minutes@1\n[^3]: E06:segment:seg-novak-3@1\n\n## Credits\n\n- Written by Ines Varga (writer)\n",
   "fountain": "Title: The Larkmoor Fund (short film)\nCredit: Written by Ines Varga\nSource: E09:document:bb33fbe8-5c1e-4f59-a745-758ed8ee520a@1\nNotes: factual work published as Example Desk\n\n.COUNCIL ARCHIVE — DAY\n\n!The ledger lies open on the archive table.\n\n!SHOT 1 — close — 5s: Slow move across ledger page 14\n[[assets: E05:evidence_version:ev-ledger@1]]\n\n[[verified_fact; sources: E07:claim:c-ledger@2]]\n\n@NARRATOR (V.O.)\nOne transfer of thirty one thousand has no receipt.\n\n[[verified_fact; sources: E07:claim:c-ledger@2]]\n\n!SUPER: 31,000 unaccounted\n\n[[verified_fact; sources: E07:claim:c-ledger@2]]\n\n.PUMP HOUSE — NIGHT\n\n!A man counts sandbags by lamplight.\n\n!SHOT 1 — 4s: Sandbags stacked against the door\n\n!Disclosure (reconstruction): Staged reconstruction of the night at the pump house.\n\n[[reconstruction; sources: E05:evidence_version:ev-minutes@1]]\n\n@SHOPKEEPER\nWe were told the fund was full.\n\n[[attributed_testimony; attributed: Mirela Novak, shopkeeper; sources: E06:segment:seg-novak-3@1]]\n"
