   "markdown": "# Follow the Larkmoor Money\n\n*documentary · factual · published as Example Desk · E09:document:f7301417-baed-442a-a5a6-1b49a762fe38@1 · draft*\n\n### Node start [verified_fact] [^1]\n\nThe relief fund collected sixty thousand. You have one afternoon in the archive.\n\n- Open the ledger → ledger\n- Ask the treasurer → treasurer\n\n### Node ledger [verified_fact] [^1]\n\nOne transfer of 31,000 has no receipt.\n\n- Ask the treasurer about it → treasurer\n\n### Node treasurer [reconstruction] [^2]\n\nTomas Brandt counts the sandbags twice before he answers.\n\n- Show him the ledger entry → answer\n- Thank him and leave → open\n\n> Disclosure (reconstruction): This meeting is reconstructed from committee minutes; the wording is approximate.\n\n### Node answer (ending) [allegation — Tomas Brandt, treasurer]\n\nHe says the receipt was lost in the flood.\n\n### Node open (ending) [invention]\n\nWithout the ledger you have nothing to ask.\n\n> Disclosure (invention): This ending is invented to close the path.\n\n## Sources\n\n[^1]: E07:claim:c-ledger@2\n[^2]: E05:evidence_version:ev-minutes@1\n\n## Credits\n\n- Written by Ines Varga (writer)\n",
